>> title: Wedge Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: iceberg, bacon, blue cheese, steakhouse, no-cook
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: wedge salad, iceberg wedge, blue cheese wedge, steakhouse wedge, lettuce wedge, quarter wedge
>> pairs-with: blue-cheese-dressing, ranch-dressing
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: narrow — the wedge has to be cold enough to sweat, and a head left out on the bench never gets there again inside the hour

>> step: render 10 min
Render @thick-cut bacon{4%slices}(cut in 1/2-in lardons) in a cold #skillet{} over medium heat for ~render{10%min}, until the fat is gone out of them and the pieces rattle.

>> step: pickle 20 min
Pickle @shallot{1%large}(sliced in thin rings) in @red wine vinegar{1/4%cup}(60 mL) with @sugar{1%tsp} and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} for ~stand{20%min}.

>> step: quarter through the core
Quarter @iceberg lettuce{1%head}(cored, chilled hard for an hour) straight down through the stem so each quarter holds together.

>> step: spoon over
Spoon @blue cheese dressing{3/4%cup}(180 mL; cold, from the drawer) over @&(~1)wedges{} and scatter @&(~3)rendered lardons{}, @&(~2)pickled shallots{}, @blue cheese{2%oz}(60 g; crumbled), @chives{2%Tbs}(sliced thin) and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} across them.

Poured and never tossed. A wedge that has sat dressed is a bowl of cold soup with a lettuce in it.
